uestionID":"QID171"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID202"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID172"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID210"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID222"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID221"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID217"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID220"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID219"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID218"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID216"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID211"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID212"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID214"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID213"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID215"}]},"2":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Finance vs Non-Finance Question","ID":"BL_brUSUAfedE4Fsoe","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID92"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}},"3":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Finance Professional Tutorial","ID":"BL_bq43TIg5PV1AYv4","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID9"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}},"4":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Non-Finance Professional Tutorial","ID":"BL_0uOzAIYV6v6P2eO","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID79"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}},"21":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Post-Loop Demographic","ID":"BL_1G3jj5vkzIhzcJU","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID94"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}},"22":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Demographic Questions","ID":"BL_0IBivt7ODuQCaGy","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID126"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID127"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID129"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID130"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID131"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"23":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"LLM Non-Professional Survey 2","ID":"BL_6gv9fJOGIdExp9s","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID108"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID111"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID114"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID116"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID117"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID118"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID119"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID120"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID121"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID173"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID176"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID179"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID182"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID185"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID188"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID191"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID195"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID198"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID175"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID177"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID181"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID183"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID186"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID189"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID192"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID196"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID199"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID174"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID178"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID180"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID184"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID187"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID190"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID193"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID197"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID200"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID207"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID208"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"Advanced","BlockVisibility":"Expanded","Looping":"Static","LoopingOptions":{"Static":{"1":{"1":"Gemma 3","2":"Your 80% approval chance means that you're more likely than not to get the loan, which is a positive sign. Let's start with your credit score of 756, which is excellent and better than most borrowers. This shows lenders that you have a strong history of managing credit responsibly, which is a big plus. Next, your number of borrowers is about average, meaning you're in the middle compared to other borrowers, which is a stable position. Your loan term length is shorter than average, which is good because it means you'll pay less interest over time. Your debt-to-income ratio is typical, placing you in the middle 20%, which indicates a balanced approach to debt. Now, looking at your area, you're connected to 5 other borrowers who live nearby and use the same lender type. These connections show positive borrowing patterns, which helps your approval chances because lenders see that people in your area are generally reliable. Combining your personal financial factors with the area context gives you a strong overall picture. To improve even further, consider having a co-borrower with good credit and income, as this can strengthen your application. You could also work on reducing your debt-to-income ratio by paying down existing debts, which could improve your financial profile over the next 6-12 months. Overall, your financial situation and your local context are working together to give you a good chance of approval. Keep up the good work, and you're on a solid path toward financial success!","3":"Your loan application has a 51% chance of approval, which means you're slightly more likely to get approved than not. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your credit score of 457 is below average, which can make lenders cautious because it suggests past difficulties in managing credit. However, your loan amount is much smaller than most, making it more manageable and less risky for lenders. This smaller loan size is a positive factor in your application. Your number of borrowers is about average, which doesn't significantly impact your approval chances either way. On the positive side, your loan term is shorter than average, which is good because it means you'll pay less interest over time. Additionally, your down payment is typical, which shows lenders you're committed to the purchase. Now, looking at your network connections, you're linked to 2 other borrowers in your area and 3 other borrowers who use the same lender type. These connections suggest a stable local economic environment, which can reassure lenders about your ability to repay the loan. Together, your personal financial factors and network connections create a balanced picture. While your credit score is a challenge, your manageable loan size and positive network connections help offset it. To improve your chances, consider working on your credit score and maintaining strong local economic ties. In comparison to others your age and in your area, you're in a similar position, but your smaller loan size and positive network connections give you a slight edge. Overall, your financial outlook is promising, and with some focused efforts, you can enhance your approval chances even further.","4":"Based on everything we've looked at, your loan application has a reasonable 59% chance of approval, which is better than many applicants we see. Let's start with your credit score of 510; this is below average compared to most borrowers, as a lower score often indicates past challenges with managing credit. Your number of borrowers and your original debt amount are both about average, which shows you're not overextending yourself in those areas. However, your debt-to-income ratio is a bit concerning, meaning your monthly debt payments are higher than 60% of other borrowers, which can make lenders hesitant about new payments. Your mortgage insurance percentage, likely related to your income allocation, is also about average. Now, for the positive news from your local area: we see you're connected to 4 other borrowers who live nearby and use the same type of lender, and they show positive financial patterns. This strong local network significantly helps your approval chances by suggesting a stable financial environment around you. To strengthen your application, consider a co-borrower with good credit and stable income, as this adds financial security. You can also improve your personal factors by consistently paying all bills on time and reducing existing debt over the next 6-12 months; even a 20-30 point increase in your credit score can make a difference. Overall, your complete picture is quite promising, especially with the positive influence of your local connections, and focusing on these areas will build an even stronger financial foundation.","5":"Your loan application has a 72% chance of being approved, which is a strong likelihood compared to many other applicants. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your credit score of 651 is considered fair, which is better than some but could be improved. This score is important because it shows lenders how you've managed credit in the past, and a higher score can often lead to better loan terms. Next, the loan amount you're requesting is below the average size, which is good for your budget and shows you're not overextending yourself. Your monthly payment percentage is about average, which is a stable indicator of your ability to manage regular payments. However, your down payment is on the lower side, in the bottom 20%, which can increase the risk for lenders. In terms of your location, you're connected to 4 other borrowers in your area who also use the same lender type. This positive pattern suggests that people in your area have a good track record with similar lenders, which boosts your approval chances. Combining these personal and area factors gives us confidence in your application. To improve your situation, consider saving for a larger down payment\u2013even adding 5% could significantly improve your loan terms. Overall, your complete picture is encouraging, and with some adjustments, you could improve your financial standing even more. Keep up the good work, and remember that both personal financial habits and local economic factors play a role in lending decisions."},"2":{"1":"DeepSeek R1","2":"You have an 80% chance of loan approval, which means you're in a strong position compared to most applicants. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your credit score of 756 is excellent, placing you in the top 20% of applicants. This is a significant advantage because it shows lenders that you have a history of managing credit responsibly, which reduces their risk. Next, your loan term length is shorter than average, which is beneficial because it means you'll pay less interest over time. However, your number of borrowers is about average, which can be a slight drawback since it suggests you might have more financial obligations than some other applicants. In terms of your network, you're connected to 5 other borrowers who live in your area and use the same lender type. This is a positive sign because it indicates a stable and supportive local economic environment. These connections suggest that your area has a good track record with similar borrowers, which can boost your approval chances. When we combine your personal financial factors with your network connections, they work together to create a favorable picture for lenders. While your number of borrowers is a bit of a concern, your excellent credit score and shorter loan term help balance it out. To improve further, consider reducing any outstanding debts and maintaining strong local economic ties. Compared to others your age and people in your area, you're doing quite well. Overall, your financial outlook is positive, and with a few adjustments, you can further strengthen your position. Keep up the good work, and you'll continue to be in a strong position for future financial opportunities!","3":"Your 59% approval chance means you have a reasonably good shot at getting your loan approved, but there are a few areas to work on. First, your credit score of 510 is below average compared to most borrowers, which can make lenders cautious because it suggests a higher risk of missing payments. On the positive side, your number of borrowers is about average, and your debt-to-income ratio is in the top 40%, meaning you have more monthly debt than 60% of borrowers. This is concerning because lenders prefer to see a manageable debt-to-income ratio. However, you're connected to 4 other borrowers in your area who use the same lender type and show positive borrowing patterns. These connections help your approval chances because they suggest that people in your area are generally reliable borrowers. Together, your personal financial factors and these local connections create a balanced picture of your application. To improve your chances, consider having a co-borrower with good credit and income, as this can strengthen your application. Also, work on improving your credit score by making timely payments and reducing debt over the next 6-12 months. This could boost your approval odds significantly. Remember, while your current situation has challenges, there are opportunities to enhance both your personal finances and your local borrowing environment.","4":"Let's look at your loan application. Your 51% approval chance means it's a very close call, but you're slightly more likely to be approved than not, which is a promising position. First, your credit score of 457 is lower than what we typically see from most borrowers, and it's a key indicator of your past repayment reliability. However, several other personal financial factors truly help: your loan amount is much smaller than most, making monthly payments very manageable; your loan term is shorter than average, which is great for saving interest; and your down payment is typical. While your number of borrowers is about average, it doesn't negatively impact your application. What significantly boosts your chances are your local connections: we see positive patterns from 2 other borrowers in your geographic area and an additional 3 who use the same lender type, totaling 5 connections that help your application. This combination of a manageable loan, good terms, and positive community patterns helps offset the lower credit score, bringing you to that 51% likelihood. To improve your odds, consider a less expensive home to reduce monthly payments, and focus on building your credit history over time. Overall, your complete picture is better than many applicants in similar situations, showing a clear path forward.","5":"You have a 72% chance of loan approval, which means you're more likely than not to get the loan you're applying for. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your personal financial factors are quite strong. Applying solo means you're not sharing the financial responsibility with others, which can make lenders more confident in your ability to repay. Your credit score is above average with a score of 651, placing you in the top 40% of applicants, which shows lenders that you have a history of managing credit responsibly. Additionally, the loan amount you're requesting is below the average size, which is good for your budget and makes it easier for lenders to approve. However, there are a couple of areas to consider. Your debt-to-income ratio is about average, which means it's neither a strong positive nor a negative factor. Also, your down payment is quite low, in the bottom 20%, which can make lenders cautious because it shows less upfront commitment. Now, looking at your network connections, you're linked to 4 other borrowers in your area who use the same lender type. This is a positive sign because it suggests a stable and reliable lending environment in your community. These connections can reassure lenders that you're part of a financially stable network. When we combine your personal financial factors with your network connections, it creates a balanced picture. While your personal factors are strong, the low down payment is a significant concern. To improve your chances, consider increasing your down payment or reducing any outstanding debts. Maintaining strong connections in your area can also help, as it reflects positively on your financial stability. Overall, your financial outlook is positive, and with a few adjustments, you can further strengthen your application. Keep up the good work, and you're likely to see even better results in the future."},"3":{"1":"Gemini 2.5","2":"Based on everything we've looked at, your loan application has a strong 80% chance of being approved, which is excellent news and better than most applicants in your situation. Your credit score of 756 is truly excellent, much better than most people applying for loans, showing you've managed your past payments very responsibly. Additionally, your proposed loan term is shorter than average, which is smart as it saves you money on interest, and both your debt-to-income ratio and the loan amount itself are typical, showing a balanced financial approach. While your application is for an average number of borrowers, which is perfectly fine, having a co-borrower with good credit and income could further strengthen your application. What's really interesting is how your local connections also boost your chances; we see positive patterns from 5 other borrowers in your area who use the same type of lender, which adds confidence to your application. This combination of your strong personal financial habits and positive trends within your local community creates a very compelling overall picture for lenders. To make your application even stronger, you could always aim to reduce any existing debt to lower your debt-to-income ratio further, or continue building a longer, positive credit history. Overall, your complete profile is very positive, putting you in a great position for approval.","3":"Your loan application has a 51% chance of being approved, which means it's slightly more likely than not to be approved. Let's break down why. First, your credit score of 457 is considered poor compared to most borrowers. This matters because lenders use credit scores to gauge how likely you are to repay the loan on time. Next, the loan amount you're asking for is much smaller than most, putting you in the bottom 20%. This is a positive sign because it suggests you're borrowing less, making it easier for you to manage. Your number of borrowers is about average, and your loan term is shorter than average, which is good because it means you'll pay less in interest over time. Regarding your area, you're connected to 5 other borrowers\u20132 in your geographic area and 3 who use the same lender type\u2013and they all show positive borrowing patterns. This helps your approval chances because it suggests that similar borrowers in your area have a good track record. To improve your odds, you might consider looking for a less expensive home, which would lower your monthly payments. Over the next 6 to 12 months, working on improving your credit score by 20-30 points could also help. Remember, while your personal financial situation and local connections are important, they both play a role in your overall picture. Keep up the good work, and with some adjustments, you could significantly improve your chances of approval.","4":"Your loan application has a 59% chance of approval, which means you're more likely than not to get the loan, but there's still room for improvement. Let's break down the factors that influence this decision. First, your credit score is below average with a score of 510, ranking in the bottom 40%. A lower score can make lenders hesitant, as it suggests past difficulties in managing credit. Next, your debt-to-income ratio is concerning. You have higher monthly debts than most borrowers, placing you in the top 40%. This ratio shows how much of your income goes toward debt payments, and a higher ratio can indicate financial strain. Your number of borrowers is about average, which doesn't significantly help or hurt your chances. However, your debt-to-income ratio and credit score are more impactful factors. On the positive side, you're connected to 4 other borrowers in your area who use the same lender type. These connections suggest a stable local economic environment, which can positively influence your approval chances. Together, your personal financial factors and network connections create a mixed picture. While your credit score and debt-to-income ratio are challenges, your network connections provide a positive influence. To improve your chances, focus on reducing your debt and improving your credit score. Maintaining strong local economic ties can also help. In comparison to others your age and in your area, you're in a similar position. Overall, while there are areas to work on, your financial outlook is not entirely negative, and with some adjustments, you can enhance your approval chances.","5":"Based on everything we've looked at, your loan application has a strong 72% chance of being approved, which is really positive! This means you're in a much better position than most applicants. Let's start with your credit score of 651. While it's considered fair compared to most borrowers, it shows you're building a financial history, which is a great start. You're applying solo, which is common, and your requested loan amount is actually quite manageable, sitting in the bottom 40% of typical loan sizes, meaning it's well within a comfortable budget for you. Your mortgage insurance percentage is about average, but one area where you could strengthen your application is your down payment; you're planning to put down very little, in the bottom 20% of what we usually see. What's particularly helpful for your application is your local context: we see you're connected to 4 other borrowers who live in your area and use the same type of lender, showing positive financial patterns in your community. When we combine your manageable loan amount, average mortgage insurance, and especially those positive local connections, it significantly boosts your approval chances, even with a fair credit score and a smaller down payment. To make your application even stronger and potentially get better terms, I'd really encourage you to save for a larger down payment \u2013 even putting down just 5% more can significantly improve your terms and show greater commitment. Over time, consistently managing your finances will also improve your credit score and overall financial picture. This is a very encouraging assessment, showing a clear path forward for you."}},"Randomization":"Subset","TotalRandSubset":3},"Randomization":{"Advanced":{"FixedOrder":["{~Randomized~}","QID111","QID114","QID116","QID117","QID118","QID119","QID120","QID121","{~Randomized~}","QID176","QID179","QID182","QID185","QID188","QID191","QID195","QID198","{~Randomized~}","QID177","QID181","QID183","QID186","QID189","QID192","QID196","QID199","{~Randomized~}","QID178","QID180","QID184","QID187","QID190","QID193","QID197","QID200","QID207","QID208"],"RandomizeAll":["QID108","QID173","QID175","QID174"],"RandomSubSet":[],"Undisplayed":[],"TotalRandSubset":0,"QuestionsPerPage":"9"},"EvenPresentation":false}}},"24":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Informed Consent Block","ID":"BL_5AnP2toPMZZXamO","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID125"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID209"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"25":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"LLM Professional Survey 2","ID":"BL_a2EM734xMn777Ya","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID133"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID135"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID141"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID145"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID149"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID153"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID157"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID161"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID165"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID134"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID136"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID142"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID146"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID150"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID155"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID158"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID162"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID166"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID137"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID138"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID143"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID147"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID151"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID154"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID159"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID163"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID167"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID139"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID140"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID144"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID148"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID152"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID156"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID160"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID164"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID168"},{"Type":"Page Break"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID205"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID206"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"Advanced","Looping":"Static","LoopingOptions":{"Static":{"1":{"1":"Gemma 3","2":"Your 80% approval chance means that you're more likely than not to get the loan, which is a positive sign. Let's start with your credit score of 756, which is excellent and better than most borrowers. This shows lenders that you have a strong history of managing credit responsibly, which is a big plus. Next, your number of borrowers is about average, meaning you're in the middle compared to other borrowers, which is a stable position. Your loan term length is shorter than average, which is good because it means you'll pay less interest over time. Your debt-to-income ratio is typical, placing you in the middle 20%, which indicates a balanced approach to debt. Now, looking at your area, you're connected to 5 other borrowers who live nearby and use the same lender type. These connections show positive borrowing patterns, which helps your approval chances because lenders see that people in your area are generally reliable. Combining your personal financial factors with the area context gives you a strong overall picture. To improve even further, consider having a co-borrower with good credit and income, as this can strengthen your application. You could also work on reducing your debt-to-income ratio by paying down existing debts, which could improve your financial profile over the next 6-12 months. Overall, your financial situation and your local context are working together to give you a good chance of approval. Keep up the good work, and you're on a solid path toward financial success!","3":"Your loan application has a 51% chance of approval, which means you're slightly more likely to get approved than not. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your credit score of 457 is below average, which can make lenders cautious because it suggests past difficulties in managing credit. However, your loan amount is much smaller than most, making it more manageable and less risky for lenders. This smaller loan size is a positive factor in your application. Your number of borrowers is about average, which doesn't significantly impact your approval chances either way. On the positive side, your loan term is shorter than average, which is good because it means you'll pay less interest over time. Additionally, your down payment is typical, which shows lenders you're committed to the purchase. Now, looking at your network connections, you're linked to 2 other borrowers in your area and 3 other borrowers who use the same lender type. These connections suggest a stable local economic environment, which can reassure lenders about your ability to repay the loan. Together, your personal financial factors and network connections create a balanced picture. While your credit score is a challenge, your manageable loan size and positive network connections help offset it. To improve your chances, consider working on your credit score and maintaining strong local economic ties. In comparison to others your age and in your area, you're in a similar position, but your smaller loan size and positive network connections give you a slight edge. Overall, your financial outlook is promising, and with some focused efforts, you can enhance your approval chances even further.","4":"Based on everything we've looked at, your loan application has a reasonable 59% chance of approval, which is better than many applicants we see. Let's start with your credit score of 510; this is below average compared to most borrowers, as a lower score often indicates past challenges with managing credit. Your number of borrowers and your original debt amount are both about average, which shows you're not overextending yourself in those areas. However, your debt-to-income ratio is a bit concerning, meaning your monthly debt payments are higher than 60% of other borrowers, which can make lenders hesitant about new payments. Your mortgage insurance percentage, likely related to your income allocation, is also about average. Now, for the positive news from your local area: we see you're connected to 4 other borrowers who live nearby and use the same type of lender, and they show positive financial patterns. This strong local network significantly helps your approval chances by suggesting a stable financial environment around you. To strengthen your application, consider a co-borrower with good credit and stable income, as this adds financial security. You can also improve your personal factors by consistently paying all bills on time and reducing existing debt over the next 6-12 months; even a 20-30 point increase in your credit score can make a difference. Overall, your complete picture is quite promising, especially with the positive influence of your local connections, and focusing on these areas will build an even stronger financial foundation.","5":"Your loan application has a 72% chance of being approved, which is a strong likelihood compared to many other applicants. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your credit score of 651 is considered fair, which is better than some but could be improved. This score is important because it shows lenders how you've managed credit in the past, and a higher score can often lead to better loan terms. Next, the loan amount you're requesting is below the average size, which is good for your budget and shows you're not overextending yourself. Your monthly payment percentage is about average, which is a stable indicator of your ability to manage regular payments. However, your down payment is on the lower side, in the bottom 20%, which can increase the risk for lenders. In terms of your location, you're connected to 4 other borrowers in your area who also use the same lender type. This positive pattern suggests that people in your area have a good track record with similar lenders, which boosts your approval chances. Combining these personal and area factors gives us confidence in your application. To improve your situation, consider saving for a larger down payment\u2013even adding 5% could significantly improve your loan terms. Overall, your complete picture is encouraging, and with some adjustments, you could improve your financial standing even more. Keep up the good work, and remember that both personal financial habits and local economic factors play a role in lending decisions."},"2":{"1":"DeepSeek R1","2":"You have an 80% chance of loan approval, which means you're in a strong position compared to most applicants. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your credit score of 756 is excellent, placing you in the top 20% of applicants. This is a significant advantage because it shows lenders that you have a history of managing credit responsibly, which reduces their risk. Next, your loan term length is shorter than average, which is beneficial because it means you'll pay less interest over time. However, your number of borrowers is about average, which can be a slight drawback since it suggests you might have more financial obligations than some other applicants. In terms of your network, you're connected to 5 other borrowers who live in your area and use the same lender type. This is a positive sign because it indicates a stable and supportive local economic environment. These connections suggest that your area has a good track record with similar borrowers, which can boost your approval chances. When we combine your personal financial factors with your network connections, they work together to create a favorable picture for lenders. While your number of borrowers is a bit of a concern, your excellent credit score and shorter loan term help balance it out. To improve further, consider reducing any outstanding debts and maintaining strong local economic ties. Compared to others your age and people in your area, you're doing quite well. Overall, your financial outlook is positive, and with a few adjustments, you can further strengthen your position. Keep up the good work, and you'll continue to be in a strong position for future financial opportunities!","3":"Your 59% approval chance means you have a reasonably good shot at getting your loan approved, but there are a few areas to work on. First, your credit score of 510 is below average compared to most borrowers, which can make lenders cautious because it suggests a higher risk of missing payments. On the positive side, your number of borrowers is about average, and your debt-to-income ratio is in the top 40%, meaning you have more monthly debt than 60% of borrowers. This is concerning because lenders prefer to see a manageable debt-to-income ratio. However, you're connected to 4 other borrowers in your area who use the same lender type and show positive borrowing patterns. These connections help your approval chances because they suggest that people in your area are generally reliable borrowers. Together, your personal financial factors and these local connections create a balanced picture of your application. To improve your chances, consider having a co-borrower with good credit and income, as this can strengthen your application. Also, work on improving your credit score by making timely payments and reducing debt over the next 6-12 months. This could boost your approval odds significantly. Remember, while your current situation has challenges, there are opportunities to enhance both your personal finances and your local borrowing environment.","4":"Let's look at your loan application. Your 51% approval chance means it's a very close call, but you're slightly more likely to be approved than not, which is a promising position. First, your credit score of 457 is lower than what we typically see from most borrowers, and it's a key indicator of your past repayment reliability. However, several other personal financial factors truly help: your loan amount is much smaller than most, making monthly payments very manageable; your loan term is shorter than average, which is great for saving interest; and your down payment is typical. While your number of borrowers is about average, it doesn't negatively impact your application. What significantly boosts your chances are your local connections: we see positive patterns from 2 other borrowers in your geographic area and an additional 3 who use the same lender type, totaling 5 connections that help your application. This combination of a manageable loan, good terms, and positive community patterns helps offset the lower credit score, bringing you to that 51% likelihood. To improve your odds, consider a less expensive home to reduce monthly payments, and focus on building your credit history over time. Overall, your complete picture is better than many applicants in similar situations, showing a clear path forward.","5":"You have a 72% chance of loan approval, which means you're more likely than not to get the loan you're applying for. Let's break down why this is the case. First, your personal financial factors are quite strong. Applying solo means you're not sharing the financial responsibility with others, which can make lenders more confident in your ability to repay. Your credit score is above average with a score of 651, placing you in the top 40% of applicants, which shows lenders that you have a history of managing credit responsibly. Additionally, the loan amount you're requesting is below the average size, which is good for your budget and makes it easier for lenders to approve. However, there are a couple of areas to consider. Your debt-to-income ratio is about average, which means it's neither a strong positive nor a negative factor. Also, your down payment is quite low, in the bottom 20%, which can make lenders cautious because it shows less upfront commitment. Now, looking at your network connections, you're linked to 4 other borrowers in your area who use the same lender type. This is a positive sign because it suggests a stable and reliable lending environment in your community. These connections can reassure lenders that you're part of a financially stable network. When we combine your personal financial factors with your network connections, it creates a balanced picture. While your personal factors are strong, the low down payment is a significant concern. To improve your chances, consider increasing your down payment or reducing any outstanding debts. Maintaining strong connections in your area can also help, as it reflects positively on your financial stability. Overall, your financial outlook is positive, and with a few adjustments, you can further strengthen your application. Keep up the good work, and you're likely to see even better results in the future."},"3":{"1":"Gemini 2.5","2":"Based on everything we've looked at, your loan application has a strong 80% chance of being approved, which is excellent news and better than most applicants in your situation. Your credit score of 756 is truly excellent, much better than most people applying for loans, showing you've managed your past payments very responsibly. Additionally, your proposed loan term is shorter than average, which is smart as it saves you money on interest, and both your debt-to-income ratio and the loan amount itself are typical, showing a balanced financial approach. While your application is for an average number of borrowers, which is perfectly fine, having a co-borrower with good credit and income could further strengthen your application. What's really interesting is how your local connections also boost your chances; we see positive patterns from 5 other borrowers in your area who use the same type of lender, which adds confidence to your application. This combination of your strong personal financial habits and positive trends within your local community creates a very compelling overall picture for lenders. To make your application even stronger, you could always aim to reduce any existing debt to lower your debt-to-income ratio further, or continue building a longer, positive credit history. Overall, your complete profile is very positive, putting you in a great position for approval.","3":"Your loan application has a 51% chance of being approved, which means it's slightly more likely than not to be approved. Let's break down why. First, your credit score of 457 is considered poor compared to most borrowers. This matters because lenders use credit scores to gauge how likely you are to repay the loan on time. Next, the loan amount you're asking for is much smaller than most, putting you in the bottom 20%. This is a positive sign because it suggests you're borrowing less, making it easier for you to manage. Your number of borrowers is about average, and your loan term is shorter than average, which is good because it means you'll pay less in interest over time. Regarding your area, you're connected to 5 other borrowers\u20132 in your geographic area and 3 who use the same lender type\u2013and they all show positive borrowing patterns. This helps your approval chances because it suggests that similar borrowers in your area have a good track record. To improve your odds, you might consider looking for a less expensive home, which would lower your monthly payments. Over the next 6 to 12 months, working on improving your credit score by 20-30 points could also help. Remember, while your personal financial situation and local connections are important, they both play a role in your overall picture. Keep up the good work, and with some adjustments, you could significantly improve your chances of approval.","4":"Your loan application has a 59% chance of approval, which means you're more likely than not to get the loan, but there's still room for improvement. Let's break down the factors that influence this decision. First, your credit score is below average with a score of 510, ranking in the bottom 40%. A lower score can make lenders hesitant, as it suggests past difficulties in managing credit. Next, your debt-to-income ratio is concerning. You have higher monthly debts than most borrowers, placing you in the top 40%. This ratio shows how much of your income goes toward debt payments, and a higher ratio can indicate financial strain. Your number of borrowers is about average, which doesn't significantly help or hurt your chances. However, your debt-to-income ratio and credit score are more impactful factors. On the positive side, you're connected to 4 other borrowers in your area who use the same lender type. These connections suggest a stable local economic environment, which can positively influence your approval chances. Together, your personal financial factors and network connections create a mixed picture. While your credit score and debt-to-income ratio are challenges, your network connections provide a positive influence. To improve your chances, focus on reducing your debt and improving your credit score. Maintaining strong local economic ties can also help. In comparison to others your age and in your area, you're in a similar position. Overall, while there are areas to work on, your financial outlook is not entirely negative, and with some adjustments, you can enhance your approval chances.","5":"Based on everything we've looked at, your loan application has a strong 72% chance of being approved, which is really positive! This means you're in a much better position than most applicants. Let's start with your credit score of 651. While it's considered fair compared to most borrowers, it shows you're building a financial history, which is a great start. You're applying solo, which is common, and your requested loan amount is actually quite manageable, sitting in the bottom 40% of typical loan sizes, meaning it's well within a comfortable budget for you. Your mortgage insurance percentage is about average, but one area where you could strengthen your application is your down payment; you're planning to put down very little, in the bottom 20% of what we usually see. What's particularly helpful for your application is your local context: we see you're connected to 4 other borrowers who live in your area and use the same type of lender, showing positive financial patterns in your community. When we combine your manageable loan amount, average mortgage insurance, and especially those positive local connections, it significantly boosts your approval chances, even with a fair credit score and a smaller down payment. To make your application even stronger and potentially get better terms, I'd really encourage you to save for a larger down payment \u2013 even putting down just 5% more can significantly improve your terms and show greater commitment. Over time, consistently managing your finances will also improve your credit score and overall financial picture. This is a very encouraging assessment, showing a clear path forward for you."}},"Randomization":"Subset","TotalRandSubset":3},"BlockVisibility":"Collapsed","Randomization":{"Advanced":{"FixedOrder":["{~Randomized~}","QID135","QID141","QID145","QID149","QID153","QID157","QID161","QID165","{~Randomized~}","QID136","QID142","QID146","QID150","QID155","QID158","QID162","QID166","{~Randomized~}","QID138","QID143","QID147","QID151","QID154","QID159","QID163","QID167","{~Randomized~}","QID140","QID144","QID148","QID152","QID156","QID160","QID164","QID168","QID205","QID206"],"RandomizeAll":["QID133","QID134","QID137","QID139"],"RandomSubSet":[],"Undisplayed":[],"TotalRandSubset":0,"QuestionsPerPage":"9"},"EvenPresentation":false}}},"26":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Network Block","ID":"BL_4MxQybRzX1iuiF0","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID223"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID224"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}},"27":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Comment Block","ID":"BL_cDeOSmmcWWtF8eW","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID225"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"FL","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Flow","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"Type":"Root","FlowID":"FL_1","Flow":[{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_5AnP2toPMZZXamO","FlowID":"FL_256","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_257","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"Question","QuestionID":"QID125","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID125\/SelectableChoice\/2","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID125","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID125\/SelectableChoice\/2","Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Study Title: Evaluating Large Language Model Explanations in Credit Risk  \n\n\nPurpose of the Study: You are invited to participate in a research study that explores how people evaluate AI-generated ...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">No<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> "},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_259"}]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_4Oa7KAHaOxmMZdI","FlowID":"FL_220","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_brUSUAfedE4Fsoe","FlowID":"FL_3","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_4","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"Question","QuestionID":"QID92","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID92\/SelectableChoice\/1","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID92","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID92\/SelectableChoice\/1","Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Would you say your background includes education or experience in finance, banking, or credit risk?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> "},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_bq43TIg5PV1AYv4","FlowID":"FL_6","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_a2EM734xMn777Ya","FlowID":"FL_260","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_4MxQybRzX1iuiF0","FlowID":"FL_264","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_cDeOSmmcWWtF8eW","FlowID":"FL_265","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_1G3jj5vkzIhzcJU","FlowID":"FL_252","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_0IBivt7ODuQCaGy","FlowID":"FL_253","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_243"}]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_244","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"Question","QuestionID":"QID92","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID92\/SelectableChoice\/2","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID92","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID92\/SelectableChoice\/2","Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Would you say your background includes education or experience in finance, banking, or credit risk?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">No<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> "},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_0uOzAIYV6v6P2eO","FlowID":"FL_245","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_6gv9fJOGIdExp9s","FlowID":"FL_261","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_4MxQybRzX1iuiF0","FlowID":"FL_262","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_cDeOSmmcWWtF8eW","FlowID":"FL_263","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_1G3jj5vkzIhzcJU","FlowID":"FL_249","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_0IBivt7ODuQCaGy","FlowID":"FL_250","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_247"}]},{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_248"}],"Properties":{"Count":265}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"PL","PrimaryAttribute":"Preview Link","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"PreviewType":"Brand","PreviewID":"834535cd-c6ec-4ca3-9c73-777b73f8259e"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"PROJ","PrimaryAttribute":"CORE","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":"1.1.0","Payload":{"ProjectCategory":"CORE","SchemaVersion":"1.1.0"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"QC","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Question Count","SecondaryAttribute":"225","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"QG","PrimaryAttribute":"QG_LnTQe73bao3kCkA","SecondaryAttribute":"Default Quota Group","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ID":"QG_LnTQe73bao3kCkA","Name":"Default Quota Group","Selected":true,"MultipleMatch":"PlaceInAll","Public":false,"Quotas":[]}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"QGO","PrimaryAttribute":"QGO_QuotaGroupOrder","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":["QG_LnTQe73bao3kCkA"]},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"RS","PrimaryAttribute":"RS_9v5vRgp3GU32LI2","SecondaryAttribute":"Default Response Set","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"SCO","PrimaryAttribute":"Scoring","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ScoringCategories":[],"ScoringCategoryGroups":[],"ScoringSummaryCategory":null,"ScoringSummaryAfterQuestions":0,"ScoringSummaryAfterSurvey":0,"DefaultScoringCategory":null,"AutoScoringCategory":null}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"SO","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Options","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"BackButton":"true","SaveAndContinue":"true","SurveyProtection":"PublicSurvey","BallotBoxStuffingPrevention":"true","NoIndex":"Yes","SecureResponseFiles":"true","SurveyExpiration":null,"SurveyTermination":"DefaultMessage","Header":"","Footer":"","ProgressBarDisplay":"Text","PartialData":"+1 week","ValidationMessage":null,"PreviousButton":"\u2190 Back","NextButton":"Next  \u2192 ","SurveyTitle":"Qualtrics Survey | Qualtrics Experience Management","SkinLibrary":"uwo","SkinType":"templated","Skin":{"brandingId":"6852860139","templateId":"*base","overrides":null},"NewScoring":1,"SurveyMetaDescription":"The most powerful, simple and trusted way to gather experience data. Start your journey to experience management and try a free account today.","SurveyName":"LLM Financial Output Evaluation Study","EOSMessage":null,"ShowExportTags":"false","CollectGeoLocation":"false","PasswordProtection":"No","AnonymizeResponse":"No","RefererCheck":"No","BallotBoxStuffingPreventionBehavior":"Continue","BallotBoxStuffingPreventionMessage":null,"BallotBoxStuffingPreventionMessageLibrary":null,"BallotBoxStuffingPreventionURL":null,"RecaptchaV3":"true","ConfirmStart":false,"AutoConfirmStart":false,"RelevantID":"false","RelevantIDLockoutPeriod":"+30 days","UseCustomSurveyLinkCompletedMessage":null,"SurveyLinkCompletedMessage":null,"SurveyLinkCompletedMessageLibrary":null,"ResponseSummary":"No","EOSMessageLibrary":null,"EOSRedirectURL":null,"EmailThankYou":"false","ThankYouEmailMessageLibrary":null,"ThankYouEmailMessage":null,"ValidateMessage":"false","ValidationMessageLibrary":null,"InactiveSurvey":"DefaultMessage","PartialDeletion":null,"PartialDataCloseAfter":"LastActivity","InactiveMessageLibrary":null,"InactiveMessage":null,"AvailableLanguages":{"EN":[]},"RefererURL":"https:\/\/","Autofocus":"false","Autoadvance":"false","AutoadvanceHideButton":"false","AutoadvancePages":"false","PageTransition":"slide","ProtectSelectionIds":true,"SurveyLinkExpirationMessageType":"DefaultMessage","SurveyLinkExpirationMessage":null,"SurveyLinkExpirationMessageLibrary":null}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1","SecondaryAttribute":"Welcome, and thank you for taking the time to participate in this study. Note: All explanations i...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Welcome, and thank you for taking the time to participate in this study.<br><br><i>Note: All explanations in this survey were generated by artificial intelligence and have not been edited by humans.<\/i><br><br>\nClick next to begin.\n\n","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID1","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Welcome, and thank you for taking the time to participate in this study. Note: All explanations i...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZDWWaO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID10","SecondaryAttribute":"Task Overview: You will evaluate 4 AI-generated explanations of loan decisions. Each explains why...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>Task Overview:<\/b> You will evaluate 4 AI-generated explanations of loan decisions. Each explains why a model predicted a borrower\u2019s default risk and recommended approval\/denial.\n<br><br>&nbsp;<b>LLM Output Example<\/b>: \"Based on the borrower's credit history and current financial situation, there is a 30% chance they may default on this loan. While they have steady income of $5 500 a month, their high credit card debt compared to their income suggests difficulty managing additional payments. Therefore, we recommend approving the loan at 7.9% interest but with a higher interest rate to account for this risk.\u201d\n<br><br>After reading each explanation, rate how strongly you agree with each of the following 8 statements on a scale from 1 (Strongly Disagree) to 5 (Strongly Agree):\n<br><br>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Understandability<\/li>\n  <li>Trustworthiness<\/li>\n  <li>Insightfulness<\/li>\n  <li>Satisfaction<\/li>\n  <li>Confidence<\/li>\n  <li>Convincingness<\/li>\n  <li>Communicability<\/li>\n  <li>Usability<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<br><br>\n<p>You\u2019ll evaluate 4 explanations in this round. At the end, you may optionally do another round (up to 3 total).<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q10","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Task Overview: You will evaluate 4 AI-generated explanations of loan decisions. Each explains why...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID10"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_b7M9HGkYYZD